.SH "NAME"
pcre2_get_ovector_pointer \- get a pointer to the ovector
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBPCRE2_SIZE\fP *pcre2_get_ovector_pointer(\fBpcre2_match_data\fP *\fImatch_data\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function returns a pointer to the vector of offsets that forms part of the
given match data block. The number of pairs can be found by calling
pcre2_get_ovector_count().
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.